+## Also (0.5.3)
+
+All additive; nothing existing changed shape.
+
+- **Zombie-aware `AdoptedProcess::is_running`** (Unix): a process that exited and was not reaped reads as not running.
+  `AdoptedProcess::try_reap()` collects the status of an exited own child with `waitpid(WNOHANG)` (`Ok(None)` when it is
+  running, not our child, or already reaped). Do not reap a process an `OwnedChild` or `std` `Child` still owns.
+- **`OwnedCommand::output(timeout, max_bytes)`, `output_with_stdin(bytes, timeout, max_bytes)`, `status(timeout)` and
+  `status_with_timeout(timeout)`** are `Command::output` / `status` with a deadline (the tree is terminated at it) and
+  bounded capture. `run_with_stdin(program, args, bytes, &RunOptions)` feeds stdin to `run`.
+- **`StderrTail::plain_split` / `capture_split` / `try_capture_split` with `LineSplit::NewlineOrCarriageReturn`** make
+  each `\r`-redrawn progress update (yt-dlp, ffmpeg) its own line.
+- **`ProcessQuery::exe_prefix(dir)`** (executable at or below a directory, by components) and
+  **`ProcessQuery::arg_containing_ignore_case(needle)`**.
+- **`AdoptedIdentity::request_quit()` / `AdoptedProcess::request_quit()`** ask an application to quit: `WM_CLOSE` to its
+  top-level windows (Windows), a `kAEQuitApplication` Apple event (macOS, may need Automation permission), `SIGTERM`
+  elsewhere.
+- **`process_usage_of(pid)`** reports another process's resident memory, commit (`footprint_bytes`), CPU time and disk
+  bytes; **`process_usage_ext_of(pid)`** adds the **thread count** (`ProcessUsageExt`); **`soak_sample(pid,
+  &SoakOptions, &mut writer)`** writes those samples as NDJSON at an interval until a bound, a stop flag, or the
+  process exits.
+- **`process_tree_usage()` / `process_tree_usage_of(pid)` / `sum_process_tree`** sum the working sets of a process and all
+  its descendants from one `process_table()` snapshot.
+- **`AdoptedIdentity::terminate_tree(options)`** stops a tree this program did not spawn (group TERM, grace, KILL, then an
+  identity-checked sweep) and reports `confirmed_gone`; **`AdoptedIdentity::children()`** lists direct children;
+  **`process_group_exists`**, **`wait_process_group_gone`**, `tokio_support::{process_group_exists, wait_group_gone}` and
+  `WindowsJob::{active_process_count, is_empty}` confirm a tree is gone.
+- **`WindowsJob::contain_current_process_allowing_breakaway()`** and `WindowsJobBuilder::breakaway_ok(true)` keep
+  `JOB_OBJECT_LIMIT_BREAKAWAY_OK` so one deliberately detached child can break away.
+
